 # Linux Basics

   Command - What it does

   pwd	- Print current directory

   ls -la -	List all files (incl. hidden) with details

   cd path/	- Change directory

   mkdir -p a/b/c -	Create nested directories in one go

   cp file1 file2 -	Copy
   mv file1 newname	- Move / rename

   rm file / rm -rf dir/ -	Delete file / delete directory recursively force (careful — no undo)

   cat file -	Print file contents
   less file -	Scroll through a large file
   tail -f app.log -	Follow a log file live as it's written
   head -n 50 file -	First 50 lines

   grep -rn "TODO" . -	Search text recursively, show line numbers

   find . -name "*.java" -	Find files by pattern

   chmod +x script.sh	- Make a file executable

   `ps aux -	grep java`

   kill -9 <pid> -	Force-kill a process

   lsof -i :8080 -	Find what process is using port 8080

   df -h	- Disk space usage

   top / htop -	Live CPU/memory usage

   curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api -d '{"a":1}' -H "Content-Type: application/json"	- Send an HTTP request
                                                                                              from the terminal
   echo $PATH	- Print an environment variable

   export VAR=value  -	Set an environment variable for the session

   `history -	grep docker`

   `command1 -	command2`

   command > out.txt / command >> out.txt	- Redirect output to a file (overwrite / append)
